  "source_name": "https://www.whattoexpect.com/baby-names/unisex-baby-names/",
  "source_type": "website",
  "structure": {
    "block_count": 72,
    "blocks": [
      {
        "block_id": "block_000000",
        "block_index": 0,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h1",
        "text": "25 Unisex Baby Names You'll Love",
        "text_sha256": "b6444369fbbea22a82d93fc41fa07f195ac235580ba6092124920ae7bd9e1808",
        "word_count": 6
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000001",
        "block_index": 1,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Light copy updates and fact-checked for accuracy.",
        "text_sha256": "d0f96820af57c1731130b2ea25ccbfb3f8c5e4f9edad0fd91b9ee33550de3a13",
        "word_count": 7
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000002",
        "block_index": 2,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Unisex baby names gender-neutral names",
        "text_sha256": "c29aeb20acf75bc6d21c350252ee161033e7167559ca526b9a516a01b2042440",
        "word_count": 5
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000003",
        "block_index": 3,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Searching for the perfect gender-neutral name for your little one? Check out the top unisex baby names here.",
        "text_sha256": "44605bf3c38de76c0c489e12fdb62d4742aa2e83b8d62803a3a909307e3e6522",
        "word_count": 18
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000004",
        "block_index": 4,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "These days, gender reveals are an increasingly popular way to find out your baby's sex and announce it to the world. But if you’re one of those parents who would prefer to be surprised in the delivery room rather than in front of friends and family while cutting cake, these unisex names will save you a lot of in-the-moment deliberation and stress.",
        "text_sha256": "944670f68d0eae0d78c08df66402481a6033a09030791dda622a48fb68d22dcc",
        "word_count": 62
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000005",
        "block_index": 5,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Plus, you might be surprised: Many monikers that have traditionally been thought of as a boy or girl name make a great gender-neutral name, too. You’ll love seeing how so-called boy’s names work for a baby girl, and vice versa — sometimes all it takes is one creative parent (or a famous celebrity) to change the perspective.",
        "text_sha256": "4936085b94df48686ac7b875d97f9ce87ea86f2c3b9481bbe3f48a1c13b98983",
        "word_count": 57
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000006",
        "block_index": 6,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Here, some of our favorite unisex baby names for a baby boy or a baby girl. You can't go wrong with any of these gender-neutral ideas.",
        "text_sha256": "4ac21983c2dfc564bfcae7be3be74c8b159694df702888c9f5f000dea5765dd1",
        "word_count": 26
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000007",
        "block_index": 7,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "1. Alex",
        "text_sha256": "8106bc6adb531ea57bf665eb0bf83df3a310f53b2b16e290809c531469550eb3",
        "word_count": 2
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000008",
        "block_index": 8,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "The variations of this classic unisex name can be written a few different ways on your child's birth certificate: Alex is, of course, a go-to nickname for Alexandra and Alexander, but it can also be shortened from Alexis, Alexia, Alexa, or Alexandria — or simply opt for Alex on its own.",
        "text_sha256": "0d2b0fef9e7b9f21e58cd7653579b97c946042eb1c4c08541e355ab66e65d49e",
        "word_count": 51
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000009",
        "block_index": 9,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "2. James",
        "text_sha256": "e474735889bbd836facc51ba581634a881577dee0022a6d43ef3a96f4e1e8909",
        "word_count": 2
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000010",
        "block_index": 10,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "You might not have considered the name James as being gender-neutral until actress Blake Lively gave her daughter the name in 2017. Nicknames like Jim or Jimmy work well for a boy, while Jamie is a sweet option for a girl.",
        "text_sha256": "724e307811bc4855ac4b7fa3ba4cf41d31230fb459b33028408d64e00b601e11",
        "word_count": 41
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000011",
        "block_index": 11,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "3. Blake",
        "text_sha256": "8fe3884dfb01ffd7720f60ab8bed0bbfffd3bbad367162fa1114049b967d8d21",
        "word_count": 2
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000012",
        "block_index": 12,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Much like her daughter, Blake Lively knows what it’s like to navigate the world with a unisex name. Blake is a popular unisex name for both boys and girls, landing number 265 on the Social Security Administration's (SSA) list of top names in 2024 for boys, and 210 the same year for girls.[1]#1",
        "text_sha256": "cbf6e5bc135d19462172f74bb4248f1f8a48915cb1bb22bb1db48c38947bda9b",
        "word_count": 53
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000013",
        "block_index": 13,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "4. Kyle",
        "text_sha256": "dfd3360fcf6828c68981ebe0409abfd65f34cbbd0247c91baba0423d588de9f5",
        "word_count": 2
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000014",
        "block_index": 14,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Real Housewives fans will instantly recognize where the inspiration for this unisex baby name comes from: Kyle Richards of the Beverly Hills cast.",
        "text_sha256": "53b225522d42a5558783717b7f7bc9a562e1edf12d7fb297c7ff25a85ca662d7",
        "word_count": 23
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000015",
        "block_index": 15,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "5. Drew",
        "text_sha256": "08dd21a7c6b790526af4ac4cfec256ae4be35d38a4bb951c88fcb51650a301a8",
        "word_count": 2
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000016",
        "block_index": 16,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Drew Barrymore, Drew Carey, Drew Brees. This four-letter name is easy to pronounce, easy to spell and easy to choose, whether you're expecting a boy or a girl.",
        "text_sha256": "c251549d08fe3610e6d77d2676e7932ab091318064aa60543165f76294fcb4ff",
        "word_count": 28
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000017",
        "block_index": 17,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "6. Taylor",
        "text_sha256": "fd305e6efa0592d43761eef38d67b75071640855c7a85b757cb5b793dfff3e18",
        "word_count": 2
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000018",
        "block_index": 18,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Another old-school favorite unisex baby name that has stood the test of time. Not only does the name Taylor work for both girls and boys, but it’s a common surname, too.",
        "text_sha256": "079c30bba814ce9b0ca3d3eef99658386a8a5b68823b14e9981c808ab0416c42",
        "word_count": 31
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000019",
        "block_index": 19,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "7. Kennedy",
        "text_sha256": "036451a3b21848f4a8e6f33c3d52974f8bbcd1920fe8c574ada95ba3135f0d5c",
        "word_count": 2
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000020",
        "block_index": 20,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Although currently more popular for girls than boys — the name took spot 89 on the SSA's 2024 list for girls, but was not in the top 1,000 for boys — Kennedy is a noble name perfect for a natural-born leader.",
        "text_sha256": "791f76c9387135c55533386677a43d2afb0d78360080119ccc0796ed982af8ca",
        "word_count": 41
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000021",
        "block_index": 21,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "8. Jordan",
        "text_sha256": "9d072224b08e3c3e901eaa5078392a82b4958e6f1ea8de81ecc75b3d726dafc1",
        "word_count": 2
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000022",
        "block_index": 22,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Jordan is a classic gender-neutral baby name, nabbing spot 539 in 2024 for girls and 104 for boys. Celebrities like Jordan Sparks and Jordan Peele come to mind.",
        "text_sha256": "98119c59729464b2fd0809e817a81e3f52ec8e06bf62918f1788f16a155df4a2",
        "word_count": 28
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000023",
        "block_index": 23,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "9. Parker",
        "text_sha256": "3977e75664378291223445de23302c26f34756cad6185246029c408935b885fa",
        "word_count": 2
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000024",
        "block_index": 24,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Parker is one of those charming gender-neutral names that works just as well in the baby years as it does into adulthood. Plus, it sounds perfect alongside basically any middle or last name.",
        "text_sha256": "fb26f5c67585ddd4be691da6a67f7cd791fe9307282ac20fd6e2de6121a4328a",
        "word_count": 33
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000025",
        "block_index": 25,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "10. Avery",
        "text_sha256": "79bbd0257ce1a7373dd0b6f9c9ac6e85bdb074c01924815c584dc89bd5a2bc14",
        "word_count": 2
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000026",
        "block_index": 26,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "This unisex baby name was one of the most popular names for girls in 2024, landing spot 31, but works equally well for boys (it nabbed spot 259 that same year).",
        "text_sha256": "152c02299c6ebc79a428b3fa9c09a5e479607fa2195cc0d405d2e8a5531f4f91",
        "word_count": 31
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000027",
        "block_index": 27,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "11. Ryan",
        "text_sha256": "19905bb7757b2fc004f6bc4115efdb88c699b49ecc71deef91f165f3dd15b737",
        "word_count": 2
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000028",
        "block_index": 28,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Ryan might seem like a boy’s name, but it's become more popular over the past few years for baby girls. You can also choose an alternate spelling, such as Rhyan or Ryann.",
        "text_sha256": "14a1c3fedfe5615214c7fb70b08e6683ef4e10553f932f7a9ba7ede10941a707",
        "word_count": 32
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000029",
        "block_index": 29,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "12. Brooklyn",
        "text_sha256": "3c48e36bf177e10e5bb8f74b900b1bf409224c8b1c832955d5f4456f29defc4e",
        "word_count": 2
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000030",
        "block_index": 30,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Brooklyn Decker rocks her name, and Brooklyn Beckham sure does, too. This location-inspired name is a no-brainer.",
        "text_sha256": "4d1722a348928b68520c949db38c4e610de572e707a022df803f16b9e3493d90",
        "word_count": 17
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000031",
        "block_index": 31,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "13. Cameron",
        "text_sha256": "8475753caa7a9941a66eba49ab6a60c556dc52edbe7192313825e6c16112e174",
        "word_count": 2
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000032",
        "block_index": 32,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Cameron Diaz is one famous Cameron, but this unisex baby name works also works well for boys. Plus, the nickname Cam couldn’t be cuter.",
        "text_sha256": "355291309c4745eee0915bb3c66f30c476f1ce575438ef2732434809c95e88e7",
        "word_count": 24
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000033",
        "block_index": 33,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "14. Logan",
        "text_sha256": "be0f79aeed23f5675df5ead0be38d82ebaac9210e9559655ba79d78a5290e10d",
        "word_count": 2
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000034",
        "block_index": 34,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Although often thought of as a boy’s name, Logan is absolutely a unisex baby name that has an equally nice ring for any lucky little girl.",
        "text_sha256": "0fdbd9b797035d06b4a95b87271985cc290bf1f9d994149a09c1931ed67c3adb",
        "word_count": 26
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000035",
        "block_index": 35,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "15. Emerson",
        "text_sha256": "c99bae2657beab0353b16c5aafd916385acd8e8f2aaad33dd40401926d240b62",
        "word_count": 2
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000036",
        "block_index": 36,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Perhaps this baby will be a creative like his or her philosopher namesake: Ralph Waldo Emerson. Consider this unisex baby name if you envision raising a free thinker.",
        "text_sha256": "0f51eb85711f98d1718f75abb9832a5004087ed411a9644ff047cad597d631ea",
        "word_count": 28
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000037",
        "block_index": 37,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "16. Charlie",
        "text_sha256": "da0723eaf7848774dabb57f9440d31d017058d50117eb4764a9ccabb4a1601bf",
        "word_count": 2
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000038",
        "block_index": 38,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "More and more, this now-unisex baby name is being used for girls. Think: Rebecca Romijn’s daughter with husband Jerry O'Connell. Charly or Charley are sometimes used as alternate spellings.",
        "text_sha256": "61e553f370be5d6eafbf13a0aeb084482df9b7686fa3436b8542dd1acf9f3ef0",
        "word_count": 29
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000039",
        "block_index": 39,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "17. Ezra",
        "text_sha256": "26e6c1f56f0a1af843f40f4f12b71ec02cc087f6bf567d5e851b57f1055527b4",
        "word_count": 2
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000040",
        "block_index": 40,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "This unisex baby name also made our list of the top hipster baby names , and for good reason. Ezra works perfectly for a boy or girl, is easy to spell and blends seamlessly with many middle or last names.",
        "text_sha256": "d1a4513a2601463f0be54077d8b12db3864e44c91b71bb342b9f92ea1a04f67d",
        "word_count": 40
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000041",
        "block_index": 41,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "18. Austin",
        "text_sha256": "29992e0554980914c393421e911a1541840c5b4e45140c4d2d0aeb75183c8ff9",
        "word_count": 2
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000042",
        "block_index": 42,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Another city-inspired unisex baby name, Austin is a great choice for a girl or boy — living in Texas not required.",
